SDL video backend: present every decoded frame (latency buffer 2 -> 1)

SDL_BUFFER_FRAMES is how many frames may be in flight between the decode
callback and SDL_RenderPresent. At 2 the SDL loop skips a frame whenever the
previous one has not been presented yet, which costs up to one frame interval
(~16.7 ms at 60 fps) of added client latency. The constant feeds ffmpeg_init's
frame ring (src/video/sdl.c) and the skip check in sdl_loop (src/sdl.c), so
changing it here changes both.

Applies to moonlight-embedded 274d3db34da764344a7a402ee74e6080350ac0cd.

diff --git a/src/sdl.h b/src/sdl.h
index 65345ba..883431c 100644
--- a/src/sdl.h
+++ b/src/sdl.h
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 
 #define SDL_CODE_FRAME 0
 
-#define SDL_BUFFER_FRAMES 2
+#define SDL_BUFFER_FRAMES 1
 
 void sdl_init(int width, int height, bool fullscreen);
 void sdl_loop();
